      <description>In the first two years of his second term, President Donald Trump has benefited from his Republican Party holding majorities in both chambers of Congress. Republican control of the White House and Congress allowed the party to pass a sweeping tax-cut measure in 2025. With party faithful running congressional committees, Trump and his administration have largely been insulated from tough scrutiny from such bodies.</description>
